        "title": "Historic Dyeing and Textile Traditions",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The history of dyeing is inseparable from the history of trade, empire, and chemical discovery. Specific dyes and techniques emerged in specific ecologies (Murex snails in the Mediterranean, cochineal on Mexican cacti, indigo in tropical Asia), diffused along trade routes, and became embedded in cultural practices that persist or have been consciously revived."
